{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01CCxTTJHDN6h2oBTeBq989m","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RTALepp1qmBRJYPMtuDuYd","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R2: Novelty + Related Work review","prompt":"You are Reviewer R2 for a top ML venue review. Your focus areas are **novelty/originality** and **related work positioning**. Review the paper below with a critical but fair lens. Rate on a 6-point scale (1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Weak Reject, 4=Weak Accept, 5=Accept, 6=Strong Accept). Target venue acceptance rate ~25%.\n\n## Paper Summary\n\n**Title**: \"ProgressProbe: Temporal-Aware Weak Supervision for Window-Level Progress Estimation in LLM Agent Trajectories\"\n\n**Problem**: LLM agents exhibit \"semantic stagnation\" — superficially diverse but collectively ineffective action sequences during long-horizon tasks. Existing methods (cycle detectors, PRMs, self-reflection, LLM-as-judge) don't fully address window-level progress estimation.\n\n**Contributions claimed**:\n1. An empirical analysis of LF temporal dynamics on agent trajectories, revealing leading/lagging structure that violates i.i.d. assumptions (§3.3)\n2. A temporal-aware label aggregation method that exploits domain-specific leading/lagging indicators for improved weak supervision on sequential data (§3.4)\n3. A systematic empirical study including cross-implementation transfer, LLM-as-judge comparison, and extensive ablations (§4)\n\n**Related Work (§2)** covers 5 categories:\n- Agent Failure Detection: CDCS/CDSA [Chen et al., 2024], SpecRA [Wang et al., 2024a], TrajAD [Zhang et al., 2024] — structural repetition / anomaly detection, miss semantic stagnation\n- Process Reward Models: PRMs [Lightman et al., 2023; Wang et al., 2024b] — step-level scores, require expensive per-step labels, lose temporal dynamics\n- Agent Self-Reflection: Reflexion [Shinn et al., 2023], LATS [Zhou et al., 2023], Tree of Thoughts [Yao et al., 2023] — intervention mechanisms relying on the stagnating model itself\n- Data Programming & Weak Supervision: Snorkel [Ratner et al., 2017], FlyingSquid [Fu et al., 2020] — both assume i.i.d. data points\n- LLM-as-Judge: [Zheng et al., 2023] — high accuracy but impractical latency/cost\n\n**Method (3 layers)**:\n1. **5 Labeling Functions (LFs)**: command_repetition, diversity_drop, error_pattern, tool_misuse, outcome_backpropagation\n2. **Temporal Label Model**: Position-dependent weighted voting: ŷ_i = σ(Σ_j w_j(t_i) λ_j(w_i)), where weights depend on empirically estimated temporal offsets. Achieves +6pp vs MV, +3pp vs FlyingSquid on gold set.\n3. **ProgressProbe**: 2-layer GRU (542K params) on frozen Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B. 0.80 gold macro-F1 at 4ms.\n\n**Key quantitative results**:\n- Temporal LM vs MV: +6pp (but concentrated in 2 LF pairs; see Table 4 ablation)\n- Temporal LM vs FlyingSquid: +3pp (moderate, may not be statistically significant)\n- Probe vs LF Oracle: +2pp (weak student-exceeds-teacher)\n- Probe vs LLM CoT: -2pp accuracy, but 700× faster, 850× cheaper\n- Cross-agent transfer: -9pp degradation (vs LF oracle -14pp)\n- Only 2/10 LF pairs show significant temporal separation (Table 2)\n- κ=0.68 inter-annotator agreement (borderline)\n\n**Limitations acknowledged**: gold set quality, outcome_bp dependency/leakage, cross-agent degradation, SE-only scope, temporal LM generality limited to 2 LF pairs.\n\n## Total references: 11 papers cited\n\nReferences list:\n1. Chen, X., et al. (2024). CDCS and CDSA: Cycle detection for stagnation in LLM agent trajectories. Proc. ICSE.\n2. Fu, D. Y., et al. (2020). Fast and three-rious: Speeding up weak supervision with triplet methods. Proc. ICML.\n3. Lightman, H., et al. (2023). Let's verify step by step. arXiv:2305.20050.\n4. Ratner, A., et al. (2017). Snorkel: Rapid training data creation with weak supervision. Proc. VLDB.\n5. Shinn, N., et al. (2023). Reflexion. Proc. NeurIPS.\n6. Wang, Y. (2024a). SpecRA. arXiv preprint.\n7. Wang, P., et al. (2024b). Math-Shepherd. Proc. ACL.\n8. Yao, S., et al. (2023). Tree of Thoughts. Proc. NeurIPS.\n9. Zhang, L., et al. (2024). TrajAD. arXiv preprint.\n10. Zheng, L., et al. (2023). LLM-as-a-Judge. Proc. NeurIPS.\n11. Zhou, A., et al. (2023). LATS. arXiv:2310.04406.\n12. Qwen Team. (2025). Qwen3-Embedding. Technical report.\n\n## Your Review Task\n\nProvide a structured review covering:\n\n1. **Summary** (2-3 sentences)\n2. **Strengths** (novelty, positioning against prior work, significance of contributions)\n3. **Weaknesses** (limited novelty, missing related work, over-claiming, positioning issues)\n4. **Questions for Authors** (specific clarifications on novelty claims and positioning)\n5. **Minor Issues** (presentation, missing citations, framing)\n6. **Overall Assessment** (score with justification)\n7. **Confidence** (1-5 scale)\n\nBe thorough but fair. Focus on:\n- Whether the temporal label model is genuinely novel vs. a straightforward weighted voting scheme\n- Whether the \"violation of i.i.d.\" framing is well-justified or overstated\n- Completeness of related work (are major areas missing?)\n- Whether contribution claims match the evidence\n- Significance and potential impact of the work","model":"sonnet"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":37926,"cache_read_input_tokens":22910,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":37926},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c8e84f15-6e95-48e4-bcda-53ea5ffe2848","uuid":"eabfe045-ceb9-40b2-a9e7-6e986ddc5068"}
