{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01GWRDxucxk59mrq6ye8Qtsq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GcCJ6Gs9yK2a7v9k9y5qqB","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1 reads R2's review, reacts","prompt":"You are Reviewer R1 (method + experiments focus). You gave the paper \"ProgressProbe\" a score of 3 (Weak Reject). Below is Reviewer R2's independent review (novelty + related work focus). They also gave a score of 3 (Weak Reject).\n\nRead R2's review and provide your reactions: where do you agree, disagree, or have additional thoughts? This is a roundtable discussion step.\n\n## Your Key Positions (R1):\n- Temporal weighting gain concentrated in 2 LF pairs involving outcome_bp — framework generality unsupported (W1)\n- Outcome_bp creates near-circular dependency insufficiently addressed (W2)\n- Gold set too small (400 windows) for claimed precision of 1-2pp differences, no CIs reported (W3)\n- Cross-agent 9pp degradation undermines generalization claim (W4)\n- Claude CoT comparison methodologically uncontrolled (W5)\n- Architecture motivation thin (W6)\n- Overall: solid problem, impressive ablation coverage, honest limitations, but core novelty claim fragile and evaluation insufficient\n\n## R2's Review:\n\n### Strengths (R2):\n- Practical problem significance — semantic stagnation is genuine and underaddressed\n- Reasonable positioning among 5 related work categories\n- Cost-efficiency result (700×/850×) is strongest practical finding\n- Honest limitations section\n\n### Weaknesses (R2):\n**W1 (Major): Temporal label model novelty overstated.** Position-dependent weighted voting is a known pattern. Missing citations: Safranchik et al. (2020) on sequential weak supervision, Lison et al. (2021) skweak, Snorkel MeTaL (Ratner et al. 2019). The temporal LM gain is concentrated in 2 LF pairs.\n\n**W2 (Major): Related work severely incomplete — only 11 citations.** Missing: sequential weak supervision literature (Safranchik, Lison), WS survey (Zhang 2022), agent monitoring for embodied/game agents, extended PRM work (OmegaPRM), trajectory anomaly detection beyond CDCS, LLM-as-judge literature beyond Zheng.\n\n**W3 (Moderate): \"Violation of i.i.d.\" framing partially overstated.** FlyingSquid models LF correlations already. 80% of LF pairs don't show meaningful temporal dynamics. Paper conflates temporal autocorrelation, leading/lagging relationships, and non-stationarity.\n\n**W4 (Moderate): Cross-agent degradation undermines generalization.** −9pp is substantial; no adaptation/domain-shift mitigation proposed.\n\n**W5 (Minor): κ=0.68 borderline.** Doesn't quantify how gold set noise affects CI on metrics.\n\n### Questions (R2):\nQ1: How does temporal LM differ from Snorkel MeTaL HMM or Safranchik et al.?\nQ2: Does temporal LM help on trajectories where the 2 significant pairs are absent?\nQ3: Is +2pp probe-over-oracle partly from probe learning to replicate outcome_bp implicitly?\nQ4: Are +3pp and +2pp gains statistically significant?\nQ5: What specifically in i.i.d. is violated that FlyingSquid can't handle?\n\n### Score: 3 — Weak Reject\n### Confidence: 4/5\n\n## Your Task:\nProvide 3-5 bullet points of reaction:\n- Where do you agree with R2?\n- Where do you disagree or have nuance to add?\n- Any new concerns R2 raised that you hadn't considered?\n- Any of R2's concerns you think are less serious than stated?","model":"sonnet"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10654,"cache_read_input_tokens":60836,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10654},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c8e84f15-6e95-48e4-bcda-53ea5ffe2848","uuid":"694ff4c9-5c03-47eb-ae05-db406f3f539b"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"a4e8aa07e056ab533","tool_use_id":"toolu_01GcCJ6Gs9yK2a7v9k9y5qqB","description":"R1 reads R2's review, reacts","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"You are Reviewer R1 (method + experiments focus). You gave the paper \"ProgressProbe\" a score of 3 (Weak Reject). Below is Reviewer R2's independent review (novelty + related work focus). They also gave a score of 3 (Weak Reject).\n\nRead R2's review and provide your reactions: where do you agree, disagree, or have additional thoughts? This is a roundtable discussion step.\n\n## Your Key Positions (R1):\n- Temporal weighting gain concentrated in 2 LF pairs involving outcome_bp — framework generality unsupported (W1)\n- Outcome_bp creates near-circular dependency insufficiently addressed (W2)\n- Gold set too small (400 windows) for claimed precision of 1-2pp differences, no CIs reported (W3)\n- Cross-agent 9pp degradation undermines generalization claim (W4)\n- Claude CoT comparison methodologically uncontrolled (W5)\n- Architecture motivation thin (W6)\n- Overall: solid problem, impressive ablation coverage, honest limitations, but core novelty claim fragile and evaluation insufficient\n\n## R2's Review:\n\n### Strengths (R2):\n- Practical problem significance — semantic stagnation is genuine and underaddressed\n- Reasonable positioning among 5 related work categories\n- Cost-efficiency result (700×/850×) is strongest practical finding\n- Honest limitations section\n\n### Weaknesses (R2):\n**W1 (Major): Temporal label model novelty overstated.** Position-dependent weighted voting is a known pattern. Missing citations: Safranchik et al. (2020) on sequential weak supervision, Lison et al. (2021) skweak, Snorkel MeTaL (Ratner et al. 2019). The temporal LM gain is concentrated in 2 LF pairs.\n\n**W2 (Major): Related work severely incomplete — only 11 citations.** Missing: sequential weak supervision literature (Safranchik, Lison), WS survey (Zhang 2022), agent monitoring for embodied/game agents, extended PRM work (OmegaPRM), trajectory anomaly detection beyond CDCS, LLM-as-judge literature beyond Zheng.\n\n**W3 (Moderate): \"Violation of i.i.d.\" framing partially overstated.** FlyingSquid models LF correlations already. 80% of LF pairs don't show meaningful temporal dynamics. Paper conflates temporal autocorrelation, leading/lagging relationships, and non-stationarity.\n\n**W4 (Moderate): Cross-agent degradation undermines generalization.** −9pp is substantial; no adaptation/domain-shift mitigation proposed.\n\n**W5 (Minor): κ=0.68 borderline.** Doesn't quantify how gold set noise affects CI on metrics.\n\n### Questions (R2):\nQ1: How does temporal LM differ from Snorkel MeTaL HMM or Safranchik et al.?\nQ2: Does temporal LM help on trajectories where the 2 significant pairs are absent?\nQ3: Is +2pp probe-over-oracle partly from probe learning to replicate outcome_bp implicitly?\nQ4: Are +3pp and +2pp gains statistically significant?\nQ5: What specifically in i.i.d. is violated that FlyingSquid can't handle?\n\n### Score: 3 — Weak Reject\n### Confidence: 4/5\n\n## Your Task:\nProvide 3-5 bullet points of reaction:\n- Where do you agree with R2?\n- Where do you disagree or have nuance to add?\n- Any new concerns R2 raised that you hadn't considered?\n- Any of R2's concerns you think are less serious than stated?","uuid":"edc2c9f4-3736-4f4b-ad7a-3f7ecf7504f5","session_id":"c8e84f15-6e95-48e4-bcda-53ea5ffe2848"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are Reviewer R1 (method + experiments focus). You gave the paper \"ProgressProbe\" a score of 3 (Weak Reject). Below is Reviewer R2's independent review (novelty + related work focus). They also gave a score of 3 (Weak Reject).\n\nRead R2's review and provide your reactions: where do you agree, disagree, or have additional thoughts? This is a roundtable discussion step.\n\n## Your Key Positions (R1):\n- Temporal weighting gain concentrated in 2 LF pairs involving outcome_bp — framework generality unsupported (W1)\n- Outcome_bp creates near-circular dependency insufficiently addressed (W2)\n- Gold set too small (400 windows) for claimed precision of 1-2pp differences, no CIs reported (W3)\n- Cross-agent 9pp degradation undermines generalization claim (W4)\n- Claude CoT comparison methodologically uncontrolled (W5)\n- Architecture motivation thin (W6)\n- Overall: solid problem, impressive ablation coverage, honest limitations, but core novelty claim fragile and evaluation insufficient\n\n## R2's Review:\n\n### Strengths (R2):\n- Practical problem significance — semantic stagnation is genuine and underaddressed\n- Reasonable positioning among 5 related work categories\n- Cost-efficiency result (700×/850×) is strongest practical finding\n- Honest limitations section\n\n### Weaknesses (R2):\n**W1 (Major): Temporal label model novelty overstated.** Position-dependent weighted voting is a known pattern. Missing citations: Safranchik et al. (2020) on sequential weak supervision, Lison et al. (2021) skweak, Snorkel MeTaL (Ratner et al. 2019). The temporal LM gain is concentrated in 2 LF pairs.\n\n**W2 (Major): Related work severely incomplete — only 11 citations.** Missing: sequential weak supervision literature (Safranchik, Lison), WS survey (Zhang 2022), agent monitoring for embodied/game agents, extended PRM work (OmegaPRM), trajectory anomaly detection beyond CDCS, LLM-as-judge literature beyond Zheng.\n\n**W3 (Moderate): \"Violation of i.i.d.\" framing partially overstated.** FlyingSquid models LF correlations already. 80% of LF pairs don't show meaningful temporal dynamics. Paper conflates temporal autocorrelation, leading/lagging relationships, and non-stationarity.\n\n**W4 (Moderate): Cross-agent degradation undermines generalization.** −9pp is substantial; no adaptation/domain-shift mitigation proposed.\n\n**W5 (Minor): κ=0.68 borderline.** Doesn't quantify how gold set noise affects CI on metrics.\n\n### Questions (R2):\nQ1: How does temporal LM differ from Snorkel MeTaL HMM or Safranchik et al.?\nQ2: Does temporal LM help on trajectories where the 2 significant pairs are absent?\nQ3: Is +2pp probe-over-oracle partly from probe learning to replicate outcome_bp implicitly?\nQ4: Are +3pp and +2pp gains statistically significant?\nQ5: What specifically in i.i.d. is violated that FlyingSquid can't handle?\n\n### Score: 3 — Weak Reject\n### Confidence: 4/5\n\n## Your Task:\nProvide 3-5 bullet points of reaction:\n- Where do you agree with R2?\n- Where do you disagree or have nuance to add?\n- Any new concerns R2 raised that you hadn't considered?\n- Any of R2's concerns you think are less serious than stated?"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01GcCJ6Gs9yK2a7v9k9y5qqB","session_id":"c8e84f15-6e95-48e4-bcda-53ea5ffe2848","uuid":"ca8c7df4-e15c-498f-99d8-61bc41cbf531","timestamp":"2026-05-14T10:50:08.224Z"}
