tly learning to replicate outcome_bp is something I flagged structurally (my W2, circular dependency) but didn't push to this specific empirical implication. If the probe's training signal is contaminated by outcome_bp's own trajectory-end information, the \"probe exceeds oracle\" result may not be interpretable as genuine generalization. This deserves an ablation where outcome_bp is withheld from probe training entirely — its absence from the paper is a real gap R2 correctly surfaces."}],"totalDurationMs":15460,"totalTokens":15393,"totalToolUseCount":0,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6692,"cache_read_input_tokens":8110,"output_tokens":588,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6692},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":588,"cache_read_input_tokens":8110,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6692,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6692,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}}}
