{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U5UN318H6PW9aySHuAtVP5","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Roundtable Reaction — R2 on R1's Review**\n\n- **Strong agreement on W1 (temporal fragility).** R1's disaggregation demand is sharper than my framing but points at the same core problem. I flagged position-dependent weighting as known prior art; R1 shows the empirical case is even weaker than I realized — the gain traces to 2 LF pairs, possibly collapsing to \"upweight outcome_bp.\" These are complementary attacks on the same claim. Combined, this is the paper's most serious vulnerability.\n\n- **R1's W2 (outcome_bp circularity) is new to me and I consider it more serious than any single concern I raised.** A 44-50% contribution from a signal unavailable at live inference, without a train-without-outcome_bp ablation, means the headline numbers may be unachievable in deployment. This goes beyond my generalization concern (cross-agent degradation) — it questions whether the system works at all in its stated use case. I adopt this as a co-major weakness.\n\n- **Partial agreement on W3 (gold set sufficiency).** I flagged κ=0.68 as borderline; R1 adds the missing CI argument, which is the mechanically correct version of my concern. The ±3-5pp CI estimate makes the +2pp deltas noise-indistinguishable. Agree this is moderate, not minor.\n\n- **Disagreement on severity ordering.** R1 treats W5 (Claude CoT comparison) as moderate. I consider it less critical than W2 or cross-agent degradation — Claude CoT is a soft upper-bound reference, not a primary baseline. Underspecified prompts are a reporting failure, not a validity failure. R1 may be overweighting it.\n\n- **R1 does not engage with related work gaps at all** — no mention of sequential weak supervision literature (Epoxy, CAGE, sequential Dawid-Skene). My W1/W2 on prior work remain unaddressed in R1's frame. This matters for the novelty verdict independently of the empirical issues R1 raises. The two reviews together cover both dimensions; neither alone is sufficient for a full rejection argument, but combined they are."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: af8bfc336dc87ee6e (use SendMessage with to: 'af8bfc336dc87ee6e' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 15336\ntool_uses: 0\nduration_ms: 16152</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c8e84f15-6e95-48e4-bcda-53ea5ffe2848","uuid":"f6fdc8f7-4fb6-423e-9aa2-ab9a0f16b176","timestamp":"2026-05-14T10:50:42.877Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are Reviewer R2 (novelty + related work focus). You gave the paper \"ProgressProbe\" a score of 3 (Weak Reject). Below is Reviewer R1's independent review (method + experiments focus). They also gave a score of 3 (Weak Reject).\n\nRead R1's review and provide your reactions: where do you agree, disagree, or have additional thoughts? This is a roundtable discussion step.\n\n## Your Key Positions (R2):\n- Temporal label model novelty overstated — position-dependent weighting is known; missing sequential WS citations (W1)\n- Related work severely incomplete with only 11 citations (W2)\n- \"Violation of i.i.d.\" framing overstated — FlyingSquid models correlations already; 80% of LF pairs don't show temporal dynamics (W3)\n- Cross-agent degradation undermines generalization (W4)\n- κ=0.68 borderline (W5)\n\n## R1's Review:\n\n### Strengths (R1):\n- S1: Well-motivated problem with clear formulation\n- S2: Comprehensive ablation suite (20 tables) — above average for venue\n- S3: Honest limitations accounting\n- S4: Student-exceeds-teacher result well-controlled, not overclaimed\n- S5: Temporal LM formulation principled if modest\n\n### Weaknesses (R1):\n**W1 (Major): Temporal modeling claim empirically fragile.** Gain from 2 LF pairs only. \"Framework is presented at a generality that evidence doesn't support.\" May reduce to \"reweight outcome_bp higher.\" Need to disaggregate: how much is temporal weighting vs. better calibration of outcome_bp overall weight?\n\n**W2 (Major): Outcome_bp creates near-circular dependency.** Accounts for 44-50% of gap over MV. At inference time on live agents, outcome_bp unavailable. The \"last-3-only\" still contributed to training calibration. Need train-without-outcome_bp ablation, not just inference-time holdout.\n\n**W3 (Moderate): Gold set insufficient for claimed precision.** 400 windows, κ=0.68, no CIs. 95% CI on macro-F1 likely ±3-5pp, meaning +2pp differences are indistinguishable from noise. Multi-seed stability (Table 9) is on auto set, not gold.\n\n**W4 (Moderate): Cross-agent 9pp degradation undermines generalization.** Missing: pooled multi-agent training experiment. Scope should be \"agents with similar tool-calling conventions.\"\n\n**W5 (Moderate): Claude CoT comparison uncontrolled.** Model version and prompt not specified. 0.82 near gold ceiling with κ=0.68. No eval on ambiguous subset. Prompt sensitivity not explored.\n\n**W6 (Minor-Moderate): Architecture motivation thin.** Why GRU beats Transformer on k=5 not discussed. GRU+Attn +0.6pp significance not tested.\n\n### Questions (R1):\nQ1: Ablation isolating temporal weighting only on non-outcome_bp pairs\nQ2: Mixed-agent training experiment\nQ3: Bootstrap CIs on gold set comparisons\nQ4: Train-without-outcome_bp evaluation\nQ5: Error distribution on ambiguous vs. non-ambiguous windows\nQ6: Claude CoT model version and prompt details\n\n### Score: 3 — Weak Reject\n### Confidence: 4/5\n\n## Your Task:\nProvide 3-5 bullet points of reaction:\n- Where do you agree with R1?\n- Where do you disagree or have nuance to add?\n- Any new concerns R1 raised that you hadn't considered?\n- Any of R1's concerns you think are less serious than stated?","agentId":"af8bfc336dc87ee6e","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Roundtable Reaction — R2 on R1's Review**\n\n- **Strong agreement on W1 (temporal fragility).** R1's disaggregation demand is sharper than my framing but points at the same core problem. I flagged position-dependent weighting as known prior art; R1 shows the empirical case is even weaker than I realized — the gain traces to 2 LF pairs, possibly collapsing to \"upweight outcome_bp.\" These are complementary attacks on the same claim. Combined, this is the paper's most serious vulnerability.\n\n- **R1's W2 (outcome_bp circularity) is new to me and I consider it more serious than any single concern I raised.** A 44-50% contribution from a signal unavailable at live inference, without a train-without-outcome_bp ablation, means the headline numbers may be unachievable in deployment. This goes beyond my generalization concern (cross-agent degradation) — it questions whether the system works at all in its stated use case. I adopt this as a co-major weakness.\n\n- **Partial agreement on W3 (gold set sufficiency).** I flagged κ=0.68 as borderline; R1 adds the missing CI argument, which is the mechanically correct version of my concern. The ±3-5pp CI estimate makes the +2pp deltas noise-indistinguishable. Agree this is moderate, not minor.\n\n- **Disagreement on severity ordering.** R1 treats W5 (Claude CoT comparison) as moderate. I consider it less critical than W2 or cross-agent degradation — Claude CoT is a soft upper-bound reference, not a primary baseline. Underspecified prompts are a reporting failure, not a validity failure. R1 may be overweighting it.\n\n- **R1 does not engage with related work gaps at all** — no mention of sequential weak supervision literature (Epoxy, CAGE, sequential Dawid-Skene). My W1/W2 on prior work remain unaddressed in R1's frame. This matters for the novelty verdict independently of the empirical issues R1 raises. The two reviews together cover both dimensions; neither alone is sufficient for a full rejection argument, but combined they are."}],"totalDurationMs":16152,"totalTokens":15336,"totalToolUseCount":0,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6706,"cache_read_input_tokens":8110,"output_tokens":517,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6706},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":517,"cache_read_input_tokens":8110,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6706,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6706,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}}}
